A||||12||gomobile||Changing 85 to 120 speedo||||6||
Z||000000||gomobile||08-31-2001||10:20 PM||||I am thinking of making this change. If I do am I asking for trouble or is it going to be a slam dunk? Any info would be deeply appreciated.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||jelly2m8||08-31-2001||11:01 PM||||just slam dunk.<P>enjoy!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Leadfoot||08-31-2001||11:14 PM||||You might want to swap all the gauges, because as you will soon find out that the 120 gauge is backlit while the 85 gauge is frontlit, or in simple terms the 120 will be much brighter at night than the rest of the gauges.  Just my 2 cents.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||09-01-2001||06:03 AM||||Yes it's plug and play.<P>86-88, 85 mph guages are backlit. <BR>Only if you are changing an 84 or 85 do you have a lighting problem.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 09-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fiero_Freak||09-03-2001||11:09 AM||||I just bought an 85 GT.   I can just go out and find a set of 120 mph gauges and they will just plug in?  Is that correct?||||reg||1
Z||000005||mbramble||09-03-2001||11:13 AM||||Yes....||||reg||1
Z||000006||Wolfhound||09-03-2001||11:18 AM||||Yes, It will work. The calibration is in the guage it's self, but your back lighting will be different. It,s best to change the whole guage cluster or at least the speedo and tach.<BR>Coy||||reg||1
Z||000007||Sleeper||09-03-2001||02:04 PM||||who still sells the 120mph gauges? thanks<P>------------------<BR>Yellow 85 GT Auto<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels wrapped with Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Intrax lowering springs, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, West Coast Fiero Strut Tower Bar, Addco Front & Rear Swaybars, West Coast Fiero Cold-Air Intake w/ HKS Super Flow filter, Beretta brake upgrade in front, KVS Performance Slotted Rotors in rear, Earl's Steel-Braided Brake Lines, custom burnt J.E.T. super chip and MSD Blaster Coil.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||09-03-2001||02:49 PM||||I am halucenating, or did I answer the backlighting issue about 12 times in the same thread a few months ago?<P>ALL 4-cyl gauges are reflector<BR>ALL 4-cyl gauges are 85mph<BR>ALL 85 v-6 gauges are reflector<BR>ALL 85 v-6 gauges are 85mph<BR>ALL '86-'88 v-6 guages are backlit<BR>SOME '86-'88 v-6 gauges are 85mph(depending on trim level)<BR>SOME '86-'88 v-6 gauges are 120(depending on trim level)||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fiero_Freak||09-03-2001||11:08 PM||||Thank you... that's very clear....||||reg||1
Z||000010||Carrolles||09-04-2001||07:57 AM||||If I recall correctly the 120 mph gauge set has the oil pressure gauge in the auxillary gauge pod while the 85GT has the oil pressure gauge below the tach.  You'll need the aux. gauge pod to keep the oil pressure gauge.  You'll also gain a volt meter.<P>There is an old thread with pictures of whats involved in putting 120mph gauges in an 85gt.  I think it was either Batman or Monkeyman who did the writeup.  The aux gauge pod does not simply plug into the 85GT wiring harness.  The aux. gauge pod was not available until 86.  It is a simple wiring patch to make it work though.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fiero_Freak||09-04-2001||10:29 PM||||Found that article searching last night.  I'm sure it will be very helpful....although the pics weren't there.  It sounds simple enough.  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Wolfhound||09-05-2001||07:28 AM||||Fiero 56, All four cylinder gauges are not reflector. My 87 and 88 4 cylinders are all back lit. you were hallucinating.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I think the 86 was also but I,m not sure.||||reg||12
